The problem is that werebeasts are human, while beastweres are beasts.
So when you killed the werejackal, you basically had a dead human.
If you had eaten it, you would have been harassed for cannibalism,
assuming you were a human.  As the rumor goes, human sacrifice is a
very chaotic thing to do, especially at chaotic altars.
If you're already chaotic, you get a demon; if you were lawful
before, well, let's say the gods won't be pleased.
Lawful or neutral gods aren't real happy about human sacrifice on
their own altars, either.  If you happen to be a demon or maybe some
undead character, the rules are a little different.

